lib/law/accountable-attention-and-publication.json:
{"kind":"koios.publication-law","id":"accountable-attention-and-publication","purpose":"Compete for useful attention without allowing demand, compression, generation, advertising, or delivery to manufacture warrant.","invariants":["Demand may create an assignment but never evidence.","A source statement remains attributable to its source until an authorized editorial act adopts a narrower newsroom claim.","No public surface may create a factual commitment not licensed by the article, its cited evidence, its uncertainty, or a declared editorial stance.","A manuscript is not publishable unless deterministic gates clear and the latest exact-manuscript independent editorial judgment accepts it.","Corrections, clarifications, updates, and retractions must propagate to every dependent headline, article, feed, card, sitemap, metadata record, and syndication surface that Koios controls.","Audience demand, attention, advertising, revenue, provider cost, and editorial warrant are recorded as distinct facts and never substituted for one another.","Newsroom learning may propose a replay, route review, observation period, or standards review from durable outcomes; it may not itself publish, execute the replay, alter a route, or amend law.","LLMs may produce prose, images, or bounded choices; deterministic code owns serialization, digests, admission, ledgers, and publication transitions.","A provider is selected by the cheapest route that satisfies the declared quality and evidence requirements; zero marginal price never waives those requirements.","No deployment target becomes authoritative without parity evidence, an accepted resource grant, a rollback route, and an explicit cutover act.","A public privacy surface must describe the requests the exact publication artifact actually emits; suspended advertising or attention may not be described as active, and active third-party carriers may not be described as absent.","Advertising units, placements, provider requests, seller declarations, performance receipts, and revenue enter Koios only under provider-authored or provider-accepted evidence; Koios never invents ads.txt authority."],"derivedFrom":["dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/ietf-conformant-clickbait.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/accountable-attention.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/agentic-newsroom.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/claims-to-prose.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/news-topology.md"],"enforcedBy":["src/researching/writing/editing/standards.mts","src/researching/writing/editing/liss-editorial.mts","src/management/newsroom-learning.mts","src/researching/writing/editing/publishing/managing/circulating/index.mts","src/administrating/deploying/static-shadow.mts","src/administrating/deploying/static-profile-parity.mts"]}

lib/law/reported-analysis-genre-contract.json:
{"kind":"koios.genre-contract","id":"reported-analysis/v1","promise":"A timely report organized around one witnessed event, with Koios's systems interpretation visibly subordinate to and licensed by the reporting.","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":800,"maximum":1100},"minimumDistinctAssertions":15,"minimumPrimaryAssertions":15,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":55,"law":"The requested length is licensed only when the admitted packet carries enough distinct source-bound assertions to sustain it. When the budget does not clear, acquire reporting or commission a narrower genre before writer inference."},"writerPromptLaws":["Write reported analysis, not a thematic essay: the event and the people, institutions, places, dates, quantities, documents, and decisions in the sources remain the article's spine.","Before drafting, silently inventory the packet's supported claims and distinct new details; every paragraph and every section must advance at least one of them rather than restating the frame.","Treat each source as evidence only for its own actors, place, time, scope, attribution, and modality; never use thematic similarity as a bridge between different events.","Koios's systems interpretation may explain a pattern made visible by supported facts, but it may not supply an unreported causal mechanism, motive, consequence, category, or analogy.","Use straight attribution when the source is an allegation, estimate, forecast, interpretation, institutional statement, or contested claim; do not launder it into Koios's voice.","Model output is never evidence. Prefer original and named sources, preserve source motives and uncertainty, and treat consequential claims as publishable only to the extent they are corroborated by the admitted packet.","When the story criticizes a person or institution, alleges wrongdoing, or reports a dispute, represent the subject's response or state only what the admitted reporting establishes about a documented opportunity to respond; otherwise return REPORTING_NEEDED.","Avoid needless harm, sensationalism, stereotypes, unattributed opinion, and commercial influence; keep reported analysis visibly distinct from advocacy and advertising.","A headline may intensify relevance but not certainty; it names the subject before withholding an answer and preserves material attribution, uncertainty, scope, and correction state.","The lede tells the reader what happened, where, to whom, and why it matters now; do not open with a universal thesis, scene-setting abstraction, or generic collapse language.","Do not create a section unless the packet supplies a distinct factual development for it; if fewer than three sections are supportable, refuse with REPORTING_NEEDED instead of padding.","The ending must close on the most consequential supported unresolved fact, decision, deadline, conflict, or question facing the named actors; never substitute an abstract meditation for reporting.","Give readers enough factual payoff in the headline, description, summary, and lede to make an informed click or no-click decision; withhold an answer when useful, never the subject."],"gates":["event spine","paragraph-level source warrant","attribution and modality preservation","headline-body congruity","non-repetition","correction readiness","exact-manuscript independent editorial acceptance"],"derivedFrom":["dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/journalism.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/agentic-newsroom.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/circulation-surface.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/ietf-conformant-clickbait.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/accountable-attention.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/clickbait.md"]}

DETERMINISTIC SOURCE-ORIGINALITY GATE REPORT:
The deterministic source-originality gate found 3 source-shaped sentence(s).
Replay the writer against the same witnessed source packet. Use materially independent prose or an explicit, properly attributed quotation. Preserve all other warranted claims and citations, and do not refresh or replace the sources.
1. Do not reuse this draft sentence: As reported in Majority of US voters link extreme weather to climate crisis, study finds, the data indicates that 61% of likely voters believe such events have become more frequent over the last five years.
   Reconstruct its supported facts independently from https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study or use a short explicit quotation.
2. Do not reuse this draft sentence: Similar majorities pointed to the intensification of flooding and flash flooding (62%), hurricanes (59%), and severe thunderstorms or hailstorms (59%).
   Reconstruct its supported facts independently from https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study or use a short explicit quotation.
3. Do not reuse this draft sentence: Adcox suggested this reflects the immediate, pervasive nature of the phenomenon, noting that high temperatures cause more annual deaths in the US than hurricanes, tornadoes, and floods combined.
   Reconstruct its supported facts independently from https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study or use a short explicit quotation.

