{"kind":"koios-news.clean-room-claim-deck","version":1,"assignment":{"assignmentId":"environment-majority-voters-extreme-weather-climate-crisis-study-finds-360dd1df","term":"majority voters extreme weather climate crisis study finds","beat":"environment","demandStatus":"attention-pressure-not-evidence"},"genre":"service-brief/v1","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":600,"maximum":750},"licensedMaximumWords":750,"distinctAssertionCount":20,"primaryAssertionCount":20,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":90,"status":"cleared"},"claims":[{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:4","fact":"Itâ€™s a sign that attempts to suppress polarize climate concerns may not be seeing full success, said Grace Adcox, senior climate strategist at Data for Progress.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:2","fact":"Photograph: Amid Farahi/AFP/Getty Images View image in fullscreen A man tries to cool off along the National Mall in Washington earlier this month.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:10","fact":"Bar chart of a poll saying voters believe extreme weather is increasing The researchers also asked participants about whether or not specific forms of extreme weather are being â€œworsened by climate changeâ€.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:6","fact":"About 61% of likely American voters believe extreme weather events have become more frequent over the past five years, the survey from the progressive polling firm Data for Progress, shared exclusively with the Guardian, found.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:1","fact":"A man tries to cool off along the National Mall in Washington earlier this month.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:17","fact":"bar chart of a poll saying nearly half of Republicans say climate change worsens heatwaves Anthony Leiserowitz, director of the Yale Program on Climate Change Communication, said the new pollâ€™s findings are â€œvery consistentâ€ with the conclusions researchers have drawn based on Yaleâ€™s surveys , which have shown Americans are increasingly linking extreme weather to the climate crisis and want to protect workers from heat .","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:16","fact":"â€ The finding indicates that scorching conditions could provide an â€œinteresting opening salvoâ€ to speak about the climate crisis, she added.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:15","fact":"â€œThere are regional differences across experiences with extreme weather,â€ said Adcox.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:13","fact":"That could be because nearly everyone in the US has experienced unusually hot days or weeks in recent years, said Adcox.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:9","fact":"â€œClimate hushers who ignore this righteous fight should take note,â€ he told the Guardian.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:5","fact":"â€œWe started with the question of our extreme weather events increasing, because we thought [that] if we can find consensus on that, that can be an entry point to being able to have a more bipartisan conversation about climate and climate intervention,â€ she said.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:11","fact":"Majorities linked climate change to worsening wildfires (64%), droughts (63%), flooding and flash flooding (62%), hurricanes (59%), and severe thunderstorms and hailstorms (59%).","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:20","fact":"But it isnâ€™t,â€ she said, adding that a spring survey from Yale Program on Climate Change Communication found 27% of people think that the changes are mostly natural.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:3","fact":"Photograph: Amid Farahi/AFP/Getty Images Majority of US voters link extreme weather to climate crisis, study finds Top Democrat says findings show public â€˜way ahead of the politiciansâ€™ as Trump dismisses global heating as â€˜hoaxâ€™ Amid a summer of dangerous heat , drought and floods , a majority of Americans are connecting increasingly severe weather to the climate crisis, new polling shows, despite efforts by Donald Trump to dismiss global heating as a â€œcon jobâ€ and a â€œhoaxâ€.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:18","fact":"But Jennifer Marlon, a senior research scientist at Yale who also focuses on climate communications, said despite this, itâ€™s not clear if most Americans understand why exactly the climate is changing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:8","fact":"Sheldon Whitehouse, the Rhode Island senator who has long criticized Democrats for quieting their talk of global warming â€“ or â€œclimate-hushingâ€ â€“ said the new data â€œadds to the mountain of evidence that the public is way ahead of the politicians on the dire consequences of climate changeâ€.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:14","fact":"High temperatures kill more people annually in the US than hurricanes, tornadoes and floods combined.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:7","fact":"That includes 72% of Democrats, 63% of Independents, and nearly half â€“ 46% â€“ of all Republicans.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:12","fact":"But heatwaves topped the list, with 67% saying climate change is making them worse â€“ including 48% of Republicans, the highest share for any of the extreme weather events surveyed.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"},{"id":"claim:majority-of-us-voters-link-extreme-weather-to-climate-crisis-study-finds:19","fact":"â€œThis is probably the biggest misconception out there â€“ many Americans still think the warming is due to some kind of natural cycle.","sourceUrl":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/19/climate-crisis-us-voters-study","force":"alleges","attribution":"required","scope":"no broader than this source assertion","sourcePublished":"2026-07-19T11:00:26.000Z"}],"prohibitions":["do not treat the assignment, beat, requested angle, reader demand, or search term as evidence","do not combine assertions from different events into one causal or thematic factual claim","do not drop attribution or strengthen source modality","do not introduce a factual sentence that cannot name its licensing claim IDs"],"writingLaw":["Each fact card is an evidence-bearing proposition, not licensed source wording.","Do not preserve a card's syntax, sentence order, or neighboring-card order in prose.","Attribute factual paragraphs to the carried source URL and preserve the card's force.","Return REPORTING_NEEDED rather than inventing connective tissue beyond the cards."]}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KDlcwvxCMDQjIpnLbCFxhh8EB3XDNWZLxscJyOOIKSAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkduserƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;2ltJeCwxZru